<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's 1996 H1 export loans up 35 pct.</title>
<headline>Manila's 1996 H1 export loans up 35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Short-term export loans rose 35 percent to $4.35 billion in the first six months of 1996 compared with $3.22 billion in year-earlier period, the Central Bank reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The strong growth in export financing suggests that the country's export-oriented industries would continue with their robust performance in the short to medium-term secenario,&quot; Central Bank Governor Gabriel Singson said.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
